# Ship after tests

whenever we implement a new feature, and the tests pass, always push to github, and supabase if it involves the backend, then deploy to the live site.

Follow `.cursor/skills/ship-after-tests/SKILL.md`. Do not wait to be asked to commit, push, or deploy after a green test run.

**Gate (all required before any push):**

- Every test passed
- Production build succeeded
- Build log has no chunk-size warning, mixed static/dynamic import notice, or chunk-load error (those cause live-site delays)

If a chunk notice appears, optimize (`manualChunks`, lazy routes) and re-run verify. Do not raise `chunkSizeWarningLimit` to hide it. Do not push GitHub, Supabase, or Firebase until verify is clean.

- Verify: `npm run verify` (`typecheck && test && node scripts/verify-build.mjs`)
- GitHub `dev` via HTTPS: `git push https://github.com/Mweenda/room-revenue-tracker.git HEAD:dev`
- Backend (migrations / RPCs / Edge Functions): `npm run deploy:db` and function deploys as needed
- Live preview: `npm run deploy:preview` (30-day Firebase Hosting channel). Use this when the requested target is a preview.
- Production: `npm run deploy:hosting` → https://room-revenue-tracker.web.app, only when a production release is intended.

For admin authentication changes, confirm the Supabase project is active before deploying. Provision credentials only through the protected admin bootstrap, never in client code or committed files. Verify a fresh Supabase sign-in, the `is_admin` authorization check, and an authenticated dashboard data load before publishing the frontend. If Supabase or Firebase access is unavailable, stop and report which verification or deployment could not be completed; do not describe the account as provisioned or the app as deployed.
